  "content": {
    "text": "BREAKING NEWS\nOur analysts just identified a stock with the potential to be the next Nvidia. Tell us how you invest and we'll show you why it's our #1 pick. Tap here.\nCan someone give SEC Chairman Paul Atkins a call? He's needed.\nAfter the bell on Monday, SpaceX (SPCX), Elon Musk's rocket and satellite company that went public last Friday, will only release quarterly and annual financial results through its website rather than through traditional wire distribution services, reports Reuters. That, and on the website he owns, X.\nMusk famously said he wanted to \"legalize comedy,\" so he's also only releasing financial results on X, which he also owns. Hilarious.\nTo make this joke of transparency even funnier, SpaceX's market cap surpassed $3 trillion in after-hours trading on Monday. That's higher than the market cap of Amazon at $2.65 trillion and Microsoft at $2.97 trillion. If we could insert a GIF of a ripping chainsaw, we would.\nThe joke turns from good-natured to something else entirely, when you consider Amazon and Microsoft both drove over $30 billion of profit in the first quarter of this year. For SpaceX, that number was -$9 billion.\nOne stock. Nvidia-level potential. 30M+ investors trust Moby to find it first. Get the pick. Tap here.\nBut fundamentals have never really applied to meme-stock king Musk. He said it himself at the CPAC convention in 2024, stating, \"I am become meme. Yeah, pretty much.\"\nMeme-coins and meme-stocks only work with specific kind of story, which SpaceX definitely has, as well as specific kind of engineering that temporarily validates the hype until it doesn't. If you need a reminder, look up Dogecoin's price right now. SpaceX has a present float of around 4%, a very limited pool of available shares, while demand from major index providers like MSCI, Nasdaq, and Russell continue to send the stock further into orbit. SPCX hit a new all-time high of $226 Tuesday morning and is now trading around $210, opening at a set price of $135.\nOn top of that, SPCX options are now live, meaning OTM calls could send Musk's company and wealth (on paper) even higher with the possibility of a gamma squeeze. If that wasn't enough, newly arrived Fed Chair Warsh is scheduled to have his first FOMC meeting and interest rate decision on Wednesday, June 17. If he cuts, everything gets even more bullish.\nMusk's novel financial reporting strategy isn't new. He did the same thing with Tesla, so we shouldn't be too surprised, but it's unnerving that the richest man in the world, whose wealth went up in one day more than Warren Buffett's total net worth, is suddenly doing whatever he wants.\nFree markets run on disclosure. This one runs on whatever Musk feels like posting.",
    "text_blocks": [
      "BREAKING NEWS",
      "Our analysts just identified a stock with the potential to be the next Nvidia. Tell us how you invest and we'll show you why it's our #1 pick. Tap here.",
      "Can someone give SEC Chairman Paul Atkins a call? He's needed.",
      "After the bell on Monday, SpaceX (SPCX), Elon Musk's rocket and satellite company that went public last Friday, will only release quarterly and annual financial results through its website rather than through traditional wire distribution services, reports Reuters. That, and on the website he owns, X.",
      "Musk famously said he wanted to \"legalize comedy,\" so he's also only releasing financial results on X, which he also owns. Hilarious.",
      "To make this joke of transparency even funnier, SpaceX's market cap surpassed $3 trillion in after-hours trading on Monday. That's higher than the market cap of Amazon at $2.65 trillion and Microsoft at $2.97 trillion. If we could insert a GIF of a ripping chainsaw, we would.",
      "The joke turns from good-natured to something else entirely, when you consider Amazon and Microsoft both drove over $30 billion of profit in the first quarter of this year. For SpaceX, that number was -$9 billion.",
      "One stock. Nvidia-level potential. 30M+ investors trust Moby to find it first. Get the pick. Tap here.",
      "But fundamentals have never really applied to meme-stock king Musk. He said it himself at the CPAC convention in 2024, stating, \"I am become meme. Yeah, pretty much.\"",
      "Meme-coins and meme-stocks only work with specific kind of story, which SpaceX definitely has, as well as specific kind of engineering that temporarily validates the hype until it doesn't. If you need a reminder, look up Dogecoin's price right now. SpaceX has a present float of around 4%, a very limited pool of available shares, while demand from major index providers like MSCI, Nasdaq, and Russell continue to send the stock further into orbit. SPCX hit a new all-time high of $226 Tuesday morning and is now trading around $210, opening at a set price of $135.",
      "On top of that, SPCX options are now live, meaning OTM calls could send Musk's company and wealth (on paper) even higher with the possibility of a gamma squeeze. If that wasn't enough, newly arrived Fed Chair Warsh is scheduled to have his first FOMC meeting and interest rate decision on Wednesday, June 17. If he cuts, everything gets even more bullish.",
      "Musk's novel financial reporting strategy isn't new. He did the same thing with Tesla, so we shouldn't be too surprised, but it's unnerving that the richest man in the world, whose wealth went up in one day more than Warren Buffett's total net worth, is suddenly doing whatever he wants.",
      "Free markets run on disclosure. This one runs on whatever Musk feels like posting."
